-2138.  Honda's number for this recall is U23.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":13,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=18V421000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":1,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"CIVIC"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"18V663000","received":"2018-09-27","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"STEERING:ELECTRIC POWER ASSIST SYSTEM","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2017-2018 Honda Civic and CR-V vehicles.  The magnet that controls the\r\ntorque sensor output signal for the electronic power steering system may not be properly secured, allowing the magnet to become dislodged.  During a full lock turn, the dislodged magnet may cause steering assist to be applied in the opposite direction.","consequence":"The unintended steering input reduces vehicle maneuverability and increases the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Honda will notify owners, and dealers will replace the steering gearbox assembly, free of charge.  The recall began November 9, 2018.  Owners may contact Honda customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's numbers for this recall are C2N, P2O.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":54,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=18V663000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":4,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2017","make":"HONDA","model":"CR-V"},{"year":"2017","make":"HONDA","model":"CIVIC"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"CIVIC"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"CR-V"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"18V817000","received":"2018-11-16","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"EQUIPMENT:OTHER:OWNERS/SERVICE/OTHER MANUAL","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2017-2018 Honda Civic Hatchback and Civic Type R vehicles.  The owners guide in these vehicles may not have been included or  if included, the owner's guide may not have been properly provided required information.  As such, these vehicles fail to comply with the requirements of Federal Motor Vehicle Safety Standard (FMVSS) number 225, \"Child Restraint Anchorage Systems.\"","consequence":"If the information is missing or improper, it can increase the risk of injury or a crash.","remedy":"Honda will notify owners, and dealers will replace the owners information kit, free of charge.  The recall began January 9, 2019.  Owners may contact Honda customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's number for this recall is O3A.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":7016,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=18V817000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":2,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2017","make":"HONDA","model":"CIVIC"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"CIVIC"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"23V858000","received":"2023-12-19","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"FUEL SYSTEM, GASOLINE:DELIVERY:FUEL PUMP","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2013-2023 Honda Accord, Civic Coupe, Civic Sedan, Civic Hatchback, Civic Type R, CR-V, HR-V, Ridgeline, Odyssey, Acura ILX, MDX, MDX Hybrid, RDX, RLX, TLX, 2019-2022 Honda Insight, Passport, 2020 Honda CR-V Hybrid, 2018-2019 Honda Clarity PHEV, Fit, and 2015-2020 Honda Accord Hybrid, Pilot, Acura NSX vehicles.  The fuel pump inside the fuel tank may fail.","consequence":"Fuel pump failure can cause an engine stall while driving, increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Dealers will replace the fuel pump module, free of charge.  Owner letters were mailed September 6, 2024.  Owners may contact Honda customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's numbers for this recall are KGC and KGD.  This recall is an expansion of NHTSA recall numbers 21V-215 and 20V-314.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":2490460,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=23V858000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":107,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"RDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"INSIGHT"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"RLX"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"HR-V"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"ILX"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"RLX"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"CR-V"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"NSX"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"RDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"FIT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"INSIGHT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"ODYSSEY"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"HR-V"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"RLX"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"ILX"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"NSX"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":true},{"campaign":"26V332000","received":"2026-05-22","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"AIR BAGS:SENSOR:OCCUPANT CLASSIFICATION:FRONT PASSENGER","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is 